<w:document xmlns:wpc="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2010/wordprocessingCanvas" xmlns:mo="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/mac/office/2008/main" xmlns:mc="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/markup-compatibility/2006" xmlns:mv="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:mac:vml" xmlns:o="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office" xmlns:r="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships" xmlns:m="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/math" xmlns:v="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:vml" xmlns:wp14="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2010/wordprocessingDrawing" xmlns:wp="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/wordprocessingDrawing" xmlns:w10="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word" xmlns:w="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/wordprocessingml/2006/main" xmlns:w14="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2010/wordml" xmlns:wpg="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2010/wordprocessingGroup" xmlns:wpi="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2010/wordprocessingInk" xmlns:wne="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2006/wordml" xmlns:wps="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2010/wordprocessingShape" mc:Ignorable="w14 wp14"><w:body><w:p><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="Title"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t>PROTOTYPE DEFECT REPORT – NTB PLATFORM</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:r><w:t>English translation of “Rapport des anomalies du prototype – Plateforme BNT”</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:r><w:t>All original screenshots are reproduced from the source report. Text within screenshots remains in its original interface language.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="Heading1"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t>1. User Interface and Usability</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="Heading2"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t>1.1. Logo Overlap with the Home and Report Buttons</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:r><w:t>When the platform menu is displayed in French, the logo text overlaps with the “Home” button.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:spacing w:after="40"/><w:jc w:val="center"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:drawing><wp:inline xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main" xmlns:pic="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/picture"><wp:extent cx="6080760" cy="395497"/><wp:docPr id="1" name="Picture 1"/><wp:cNvGraphicFramePr><a:graphicFrameLocks noChangeAspect="1"/></wp:cNvGraphicFramePr><a:graphic><a:graphicData uri="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/picture"><pic:pic><pic:nvPicPr><pic:cNvPr id="0" name="p1_1.png"/><pic:cNvPicPr/></pic:nvPicPr><pic:blipFill><a:blip r:embed="rId9"/><a:stretch><a:fillRect/></a:stretch></pic:blipFill><pic:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="0" y="0"/><a:ext cx="6080760" cy="395497"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"/></pic:spPr></pic:pic></a:graphicData></a:graphic></wp:inline></w:drawing></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="FigureCaption"/><w:jc w:val="center"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t>Original screenshot: logo and navigation-button overlap</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="Heading2"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t>1.2. Responsive Design Issue on the Administrative Platform (Web Responsive Test)</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:r><w:t>Finding: The administrative platform interface does not adapt properly to smaller screens.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:r><w:t>When users access the platform from a tablet or mobile phone, the main navigation menu does not display correctly or is inaccessible.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:r><w:t>This issue makes navigation difficult, or even impossible, on tablets and mobile devices and prevents a consistent user experience across different screen sizes.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:r><w:t>The responsive design of the administrative platform should be reviewed so that the interface automatically adjusts to different screen resolutions.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:spacing w:after="40"/><w:jc w:val="center"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:drawing><wp:inline xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main" xmlns:pic="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/picture"><wp:extent cx="6080760" cy="3779520"/><wp:docPr id="2" name="Picture 2"/><wp:cNvGraphicFramePr><a:graphicFrameLocks noChangeAspect="1"/></wp:cNvGraphicFramePr><a:graphic><a:graphicData uri="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/picture"><pic:pic><pic:nvPicPr><pic:cNvPr id="0" name="p1_2.png"/><pic:cNvPicPr/></pic:nvPicPr><pic:blipFill><a:blip r:embed="rId10"/><a:stretch><a:fillRect/></a:stretch></pic:blipFill><pic:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="0" y="0"/><a:ext cx="6080760" cy="3779520"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"/></pic:spPr></pic:pic></a:graphicData></a:graphic></wp:inline></w:drawing></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="FigureCaption"/><w:jc w:val="center"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t>Original screenshot: mobile, tablet and desktop responsive-design test</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="Heading1"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t>2. Login Form</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="Heading2"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t>2.1. Missing Password Reset Functionality</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:r><w:t>The user login form currently has no link or button allowing a user to reset a forgotten password.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:r><w:t>Impact: A user who forgets their password has no self-service mechanism for regaining access to their account.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:r><w:t>The user must currently contact a platform administrator, who then has to use the user management interface to reset the password.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:r><w:t>Recommendation</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:r><w:t>Add a “Forgot password?” link to the login page.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:r><w:t>This link should allow users to initiate a secure password reset process themselves.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:r><w:t>The recommended process is:</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="ListNumber"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t>The user clicks “Forgot password?”.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="ListNumber"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t>The user enters their email address or username.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="ListNumber"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t>The system verifies the account.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="ListNumber"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t>A secure, temporary password reset link is sent to the email address associated with the account.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="ListNumber"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t>The user sets a new password.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="ListNumber"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t>The reset link expires after a limited period and can only be used once.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:spacing w:after="40"/><w:jc w:val="center"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:drawing><wp:inline xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main" xmlns:pic="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/picture"><wp:extent cx="6080760" cy="3240645"/><wp:docPr id="3" name="Picture 3"/><wp:cNvGraphicFramePr><a:graphicFrameLocks noChangeAspect="1"/></wp:cNvGraphicFramePr><a:graphic><a:graphicData uri="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/picture"><pic:pic><pic:nvPicPr><pic:cNvPr id="0" name="p2_1.png"/><pic:cNvPicPr/></pic:nvPicPr><pic:blipFill><a:blip r:embed="rId11"/><a:stretch><a:fillRect/></a:stretch></pic:blipFill><pic:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="0" y="0"/><a:ext cx="6080760" cy="3240645"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"/></pic:spPr></pic:pic></a:graphicData></a:graphic></wp:inline></w:drawing></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="FigureCaption"/><w:jc w:val="center"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t>Public portal: original login-screen screenshot</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:spacing w:after="40"/><w:jc w:val="center"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:drawing><wp:inline xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main" xmlns:pic="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/picture"><wp:extent cx="5806440" cy="6020612"/><wp:docPr id="4" name="Picture 4"/><wp:cNvGraphicFramePr><a:graphicFrameLocks noChangeAspect="1"/></wp:cNvGraphicFramePr><a:graphic><a:graphicData uri="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/picture"><pic:pic><pic:nvPicPr><pic:cNvPr id="0" name="p2_2.png"/><pic:cNvPicPr/></pic:nvPicPr><pic:blipFill><a:blip r:embed="rId12"/><a:stretch><a:fillRect/></a:stretch></pic:blipFill><pic:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="0" y="0"/><a:ext cx="5806440" cy="6020612"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"/></pic:spPr></pic:pic></a:graphicData></a:graphic></wp:inline></w:drawing></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="FigureCaption"/><w:jc w:val="center"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t>Administrative portal: original login-screen screenshot</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="Heading1"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t>3. Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA)</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="Heading2"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t>3.1. “Reset MFA” Button</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:spacing w:after="40"/><w:jc w:val="center"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:drawing><wp:inline xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main" xmlns:pic="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/picture"><wp:extent cx="6080760" cy="2850189"/><wp:docPr id="5" name="Picture 5"/><wp:cNvGraphicFramePr><a:graphicFrameLocks noChangeAspect="1"/></wp:cNvGraphicFramePr><a:graphic><a:graphicData uri="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/picture"><pic:pic><pic:nvPicPr><pic:cNvPr id="0" name="p3_1.png"/><pic:cNvPicPr/></pic:nvPicPr><pic:blipFill><a:blip r:embed="rId13"/><a:stretch><a:fillRect/></a:stretch></pic:blipFill><pic:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="0" y="0"/><a:ext cx="6080760" cy="2850189"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"/></pic:spPr></pic:pic></a:graphicData></a:graphic></wp:inline></w:drawing></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="FigureCaption"/><w:jc w:val="center"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t>Original screenshot: “Reset MFA” control in the user administration interface</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:r><w:t>Finding: The button currently labelled “Reset MFA” does not trigger any functional action.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="Heading2"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t>3.2. MFA Security Setting</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:spacing w:after="40"/><w:jc w:val="center"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:drawing><wp:inline xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main" xmlns:pic="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/picture"><wp:extent cx="6080760" cy="1334017"/><wp:docPr id="6" name="Picture 6"/><wp:cNvGraphicFramePr><a:graphicFrameLocks noChangeAspect="1"/></wp:cNvGraphicFramePr><a:graphic><a:graphicData uri="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/picture"><pic:pic><pic:nvPicPr><pic:cNvPr id="0" name="p3_2.png"/><pic:cNvPicPr/></pic:nvPicPr><pic:blipFill><a:blip r:embed="rId14"/><a:stretch><a:fillRect/></a:stretch></pic:blipFill><pic:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="0" y="0"/><a:ext cx="6080760" cy="1334017"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"/></pic:spPr></pic:pic></a:graphicData></a:graphic></wp:inline></w:drawing></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="FigureCaption"/><w:jc w:val="center"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t>Original screenshot: MFA security configuration and verification method</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:spacing w:after="40"/><w:jc w:val="center"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:drawing><wp:inline xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main" xmlns:pic="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/picture"><wp:extent cx="6080760" cy="1608667"/><wp:docPr id="7" name="Picture 7"/><wp:cNvGraphicFramePr><a:graphicFrameLocks noChangeAspect="1"/></wp:cNvGraphicFramePr><a:graphic><a:graphicData uri="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/picture"><pic:pic><pic:nvPicPr><pic:cNvPr id="0" name="p3_3.png"/><pic:cNvPicPr/></pic:nvPicPr><pic:blipFill><a:blip r:embed="rId15"/><a:stretch><a:fillRect/></a:stretch></pic:blipFill><pic:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="0" y="0"/><a:ext cx="6080760" cy="1608667"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"/></pic:spPr></pic:pic></a:graphicData></a:graphic></wp:inline></w:drawing></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="FigureCaption"/><w:jc w:val="center"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t>Original screenshot: MFA email verification code entry</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:r><w:t>Finding: A security setting for configuring multi-factor authentication (MFA) is present on the platform.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:r><w:t>When MFA is configured using the email OTP option, the platform displays a message stating that a six-digit verification code has been sent to the user.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:r><w:t>However, after checking, no code is actually received in the user’s email inbox.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:r><w:t>Impact: This defect prevents users from correctly completing the activation or verification of MFA using an OTP.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:r><w:t>It also creates an inconsistency between the behaviour indicated by the interface and the actual operation of the code-delivery service.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:r><w:t>The following issues must be corrected:</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="ListNumber"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t>The “Reset MFA” button does not trigger any action.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="ListNumber"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t>The six-digit OTP stated to have been sent is not received by the user.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="ListNumber"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t>The operation of the email-sending service must be verified.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="ListNumber"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t>The OTP generation, sending and validation process must be tested end to end.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="ListNumber"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t>An MFA reset procedure must be provided for users who lose access to their second authentication factor.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="Heading1"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t>4. Dialog Boxes and User Experience</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="Heading2"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t>4.1. Use of Native Browser Dialog Boxes</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:r><w:t>Finding: During certain administrative operations, particularly when generating or entering text, the system displays a native browser dialog box when the “Suspend” and “Deactivate” buttons are clicked.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:r><w:t>In the screenshot, the message also displays the server’s IP address, for example:</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:spacing w:after="40"/><w:jc w:val="center"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:drawing><wp:inline xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main" xmlns:pic="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/picture"><wp:extent cx="6080760" cy="3387852"/><wp:docPr id="8" name="Picture 8"/><wp:cNvGraphicFramePr><a:graphicFrameLocks noChangeAspect="1"/></wp:cNvGraphicFramePr><a:graphic><a:graphicData uri="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/picture"><pic:pic><pic:nvPicPr><pic:cNvPr id="0" name="p4_1.png"/><pic:cNvPicPr/></pic:nvPicPr><pic:blipFill><a:blip r:embed="rId16"/><a:stretch><a:fillRect/></a:stretch></pic:blipFill><pic:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="0" y="0"/><a:ext cx="6080760" cy="3387852"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"/></pic:spPr></pic:pic></a:graphicData></a:graphic></wp:inline></w:drawing></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="FigureCaption"/><w:jc w:val="center"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t>Original screenshot: native browser prompt displaying the server address</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:r><w:t>This behaviour gives the impression of an unfinished application and is inappropriate for an institutional platform intended for production use.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:r><w:t>I recommend replacing the window.confirm() and window.prompt() dialogs with modal dialogs integrated directly into the platform interface.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="Heading1"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t>5. Submission of NTB Complaints / Cases</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="Heading2"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t>5.1. Unable to Submit a Complaint</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:r><w:t>Finding: It is currently not possible to submit an NTB complaint/case through:</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="ListBullet"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t>The public portal;</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="ListBullet"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t>The administrative portal.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:r><w:t>This defect blocks a core platform function: recording and submitting a non-tariff barrier.</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:spacing w:after="40"/><w:jc w:val="center"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:drawing><wp:inline xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main" xmlns:pic="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/picture"><wp:extent cx="5806440" cy="5934335"/><wp:docPr id="9" name="Picture 9"/><wp:cNvGraphicFramePr><a:graphicFrameLocks noChangeAspect="1"/></wp:cNvGraphicFramePr><a:graphic><a:graphicData uri="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/picture"><pic:pic><pic:nvPicPr><pic:cNvPr id="0" name="p5_1.png"/><pic:cNvPicPr/></pic:nvPicPr><pic:blipFill><a:blip r:embed="rId17"/><a:stretch><a:fillRect/></a:stretch></pic:blipFill><pic:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="0" y="0"/><a:ext cx="5806440" cy="5934335"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"/></pic:spPr></pic:pic></a:graphicData></a:graphic></wp:inline></w:drawing></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="FigureCaption"/><w:jc w:val="center"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:t>Original screenshot: complaint submission – description stage</w:t></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:spacing w:after="40"/><w:jc w:val="center"/></w:pPr><w:r><w:drawing><wp:inline xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main" xmlns:pic="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/picture"><wp:extent cx="6080760" cy="3380581"/><wp:docPr id="10" name="Picture 10"/><wp:cNvGraphicFramePr><a:graphicFrameLocks noChangeAspect="1"/></wp:cNvGraphicFramePr><a:graphic><a:graphicData uri="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/picture"><pic:pic><pic:nvPicPr><pic:cNvPr id="0" name="p6_1.png"/><pic:cNvPicPr/></pic:nvPicPr><pic:blipFill><a:blip r:embed="rId18"/><a:stretch><a:fillRect/></a:stretch></pic:blipFill><pic:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="0" y="0"/><a:ext cx="6080760" cy="3380581"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"/></pic:spPr></pic:pic></a:graphicData></a:graphic></wp:inline></w:drawing></w:r></w:p><w:p><w:pPr><w:p